; TGUID typed constants: strings that are not '{XXXXXXXX-XXXX-XXXX-XXXX-
; XXXXXXXXXXXX}' or '' (as Free Pascal's "Improper GUID syntax"), and values
; that are not strings; DWord's range. The same in tp and objfpc.
; RUN: not %p3 --mode=tp -ferror-limit=0 -c %S/Inputs/guid-consts/errors.pas -o %t.o 2>&1 | FileCheck %s
; RUN: not %p3 --mode=objfpc -ferror-limit=0 -c %S/Inputs/guid-consts/errors.pas -o %t.o 2>&1 | FileCheck %s
; CHECK: errors.pas:4:18: error: improper GUID syntax: expected '{XXXXXXXX-XXXX-XXXX-XXXX-XXXXXXXXXXXX}' (hexadecimal digits) or ''
; CHECK: errors.pas:5:21: error: improper GUID syntax
; CHECK: errors.pas:6:19: error: improper GUID syntax
; CHECK: errors.pas:7:19: error: improper GUID syntax
; CHECK: errors.pas:8:20: error: improper GUID syntax
; CHECK: errors.pas:9:19: error: cannot initialize 'TGUID' with a value of type 'integer'
; CHECK: errors.pas:11:19: error: value -1 is out of range for 'cardinal'
; CHECK-NOT: error:
